# Local scratch
*.local

# Benchmark run output (stage 2-3).
#
# A run's raw result is regenerable and depends on whoever paid for it (key, model,
# network, day). Committing them makes the repository a place where only the good runs
# ever land — the exact self-deception `task/stage-2-4.md` forbids. The durable artefact
# is `labels.json` (a person's judgement, run-independent) plus the numbers written into
# `docs/benchmark/README.md`. Same for the generated per-run report; the template stays.
tests/benchmark/results/*
!tests/benchmark/results/.gitkeep
!tests/benchmark/results/labels.json
tests/benchmark/reports/*
!tests/benchmark/reports/.gitkeep
!tests/benchmark/reports/judgement-template.md
# The attribution write-up is an analysis, not a run: it survives any single run and it
# is the artefact stage 2-4 is judged on. Per-run reports stay ignored.
!tests/benchmark/reports/attribution-*.md

# A dogfooding record is the same kind of thing: what a person saw one pass do against a
# live page, written up after the fact, carried as evidence for a number published in the
# CHANGELOG. The run artefacts it describes stay ignored below.
!tests/benchmark/reports/dogfood-*.md

# Agent working notes (internal; never part of the public tree)
.workbuddy/

# Logo design scratch (never committed)
.logo-draft/

# Dogfooding output (stage 3-1, `pnpm dogfood`) — screenshots, the saved tool record and a
# row sample pulled off a live page. Regenerable, priced per pass, and full of page content
# that must never reach a recipe unredacted.
.dogfood/
